# Trota OS — packages that must NOT be installed by the image build.
# During the build they are pinned to priority -1 so that no Recommends can pull
# them in; tests/test_manifest.py checks that no other list contains them.
# Users remain free to install any of them later with APT.
# Format: <package>  # <reason>

ubuntu-report            # telemetry: hardware survey sent to Canonical (opt-out)
whoopsie                 # telemetry: crash report upload daemon
apport-gtk               # crash reporting UI (sends reports to Launchpad)
apport                   # crash reporting backend
kerneloops               # uploads kernel oops reports
popularity-contest       # package usage survey
cloud-init               # cloud provisioning, not useful on a desktop
gnome-remote-desktop     # remote desktop server: no remote access by default
openssh-server           # no network services listening by default
postfix                  # mail server, may be pulled by smartmontools Recommends
exim4-daemon-light       # mail server
gnome-initial-setup      # Ubuntu-branded onboarding; replaced by Trota Welcome
snapd                    # Trota OS ships no snaps (blocked also on the installed system, see trota-software-sources)
gnome-software-plugin-snap # snap support in GNOME Software
ubuntu-kernel-accessories # bpftrace, bpfcc-tools and two extra LLVM copies (~210 MB), kernel developers only
linux-tools-common       # perf and kernel tools (~170 MB with LLVM), recommended by the HWE kernel

# Note: ubuntu-wallpapers cannot be excluded because Ubuntu's gnome-shell
# package depends on it; Trota OS only changes the default wallpaper.
